### 7. Extreme Single-Day Rain Event Extraction
* **Code:**
  ```powershell
  $imergData = (Get-Content nasapower.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json).properties.parameter.IMERG_PRECTOT
  $weatherData = (Get-Content nasapower_weather.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json).properties.parameter.PRECTOTCORR

  $events = @()
  foreach ($prop in $imergData.PSObject.Properties) {
      $date = $prop.Name
      $val = [double]$prop.Value
      if ($val -ge 70) {
          $mVal = [double]$weatherData.$date
          $events += [PSCustomObject]@{
              Date = $date
              IMERG_mm = [math]::Round($val, 1)
              MERRA_mm = [math]::Round($mVal, 1)
          }
      }
  }
  $events | Sort-Object IMERG_mm -Descending | Select-Object -First 10 | Format-Table -AutoSize
  ```
* **Reason:** Identify Buea's highest single-day precipitation events in IMERG (~10 km) and contrast them with MERRA-2 (~50 km) to evaluate localized convective downpours on Mount Cameroon's slopes.
* **Result:** Discovered top IMERG downpours: 134 mm (2018-02-26), 123.9 mm (2024-07-19), 115 mm (2012-07-14), 105.4 mm (2020-09-05), and 101.5 mm (2010-05-21).

